/* book exam traps: Do not mix energy, charge and voltage: E = ½CV² gives joules, Q = CV gives coulombs, V is volts. The capacitance must be in farads, not microfarads. | A pacemaker does not pump blood. It only triggers a contraction; the heart muscle does the pumping. | Unsynchronised defibrillation is not synchronised cardioversion. Cardioversion times the shock to the R wave; defibrillation fires immediately. | Fixed-rate pacing fires at the set rate regardless of intrinsic beats; demand mode inhibits when a beat is sensed. | External defibrillation uses more energy than internal defibrillation because the current path is longer and loss is greater. */
